<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 744–714 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Piankhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piye, also known as Piankhi, was a king of Kush in the eighth century BCE and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashta">Kashta</a>. He campaigned northwards into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, overcoming its fragmented local rulers and asserting Kushite authority. His conquest began the period in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> ruled Egypt as its Twenty-fifth Dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piye.jpg" alt="Piye" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Auguste Mariette (1821-1881) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stele_Piye_Mariette.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
